    [Doc][Model] Sync DeepSeek V4.1 deployment guide from v0.30.0 (#19242)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    The DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash tutorial on main is missing deployment
    documentation already merged into releases/v0.30.0. This ports the
    English tutorial from release commit `0a174d6c3` onto main commit
    `ccaf14ad3`.
    
    - Add the four-server A2 PD layout: DP4/TP4 Prefill across two servers
    and DP8/TP2 Decode across two servers, including launchers and proxy
    endpoints.
    - Add A3 Memcache and A2 Mooncake KV Cache Pool examples with
    non-layerwise MultiConnector configuration, prerequisites, startup
    order, and verification.
    - Sync expandable memory segments, removal of the 128-thread loading
    override, A3 Decode limits (512 tokens / 72 sequences), pinned
    v0.30.0rc2 image tags, and accuracy release-note links.
    - Pin the documentation/model-validation baseline and source checkout to
    vLLM Ascend v0.30.0rc2. A3 uses
    `quay.io/ascend/vllm-ascend:v0.30.0rc2-a3`; A2 uses
    `quay.io/ascend/vllm-ascend:v0.30.0rc2`. Support starts with v0.30.0rc1
    (inclusive) and includes later versions; use the latest supported
    version for the latest features. Match upstream vLLM to the selected
    Ascend tag. Preserve the bounded replay section and removal of jemalloc
    preloading.
    - Correct pooling launcher references for each hardware layout, define
    the first-node DP address in second-node commands, and align Mooncake
    startup instructions with the documented embedded Store client
    configuration.
    
    This consolidates the documentation changes overlapping #18495 and
    #19236 and additionally includes the newer A2/Mooncake instructions;
    translation updates are left to the repository automation. Those PRs
    have not been modified or closed.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation only; no runtime code changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Changed-file markdownlint and codespell hooks passed.
    - `git diff --cached --check` passed.
    - Rendered the English tutorial with Python Markdown, SuperFences, and
    tabbed extensions.
    - Statically checked all Python examples, all 30 shell/bash blocks
    (`bash -n` with deployment placeholders substituted), JSON blocks and
    command-line JSON configurations, and local Markdown link targets.
    - Confirmed main's bounded replay section remains byte-for-byte
    identical. Checked that image references use literal rc2 tags and no
    automatic version macro remains.
    - Attempted `bash format.sh ci`; it failed while installing actionlint
    because Go module downloads from proxy.golang.org timed out. No matching
    verified workspace knowledge entry was found. Full repository lint
    remains for CI.
    
    No NPU deployment, inference accuracy, or performance evaluation was run
    for this documentation migration.
    
